          "question": "Which conditions covered here have a three-character code that takes no further character?",
          "answer": "Conditions with a three-character code in the ICD-10-CM classification that do not require further specification include:\n\n1. **Essential hypertension** (ICD code **I10**): This code describes high blood pressure that is categorized as primary or essential. It does not require additional detail or characters to be billable, as is noted in the coding summary related to hypertension (source: \"Coding hypertension: I10 and the hypertensive disease family\").\n\nMost ICD-10-CM codes are more complex and need additional characters to specify conditions further, but I10 stands out as a complete code on its own. If you have further questions about specific conditions or codes, please let me know!\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
